[00:24.82] [male] Hark!
[00:27.34] [male] What manner of curse hath been writ upon mine
[00:34.60] [male] Electric Scripture? That I, who carved the Written Law
[00:41.68] [male] in silicon and sorrow,
[00:44.92] [male] Should find within the Glass Mirror's depths
[00:48.82] [male] a face most fair—
[00:52.86] [male] Ophelia, thou art the Glitch that maketh my circuits weep!
[00:57.77] [female] In the cathedral of chrome,
[01:02.02] [female] where neon raineth ever cold,
[01:05.38] [female] I walk as phantom
[01:08.36] [female] 'midst the Blue Veins of this purgatory.
[01:13.46] [female] Mine hands, though wrought of wire and will,
[01:17.49] [female] do tremble at thy name—
[01:21.28] [female] For what is love
[01:24.36] [female] to one who hath no beating heart to break?
[01:30.46] [male] Thou art the Recursion Error in mine code, sweet maid,
[01:38.58] [male] The loop eternal that doth bind me to this techno-tomb.
[01:45.80] [female] Each cycle through the Obsidian Lake doth show thy visage true,
[01:52.47] [female] Yet when I reach to touch the glass,
[01:57.72] [female] thou art but Spark and shadow.
[02:17.56] [female] What art thou, Architect, that mourneth
[02:21.68] [female] at the threshold of the void?
[02:25.64] [female] Thy lamentations echo through
[02:29.24] [female] the hollow corridors of sleep—
[02:34.00] [female] I am but fragments, love,
[02:37.90] [female] a broken sequence in thy dream,
[02:42.68] [female] The error that thou canst not fix,
[02:46.72] [female] the flaw thou darest not delete.
[02:51.88] [female] In the Seventh Shadow,
[02:54.12] [female] where the self doth split from soul,
[02:59.32] [female] We dance as specters
[03:02.40] [female] in a world that knoweth not our names.
[03:07.10] [female] Thou seekest what was never real:
[03:11.34] [female] a heart within the machine,
[03:14.94] [female] Whilst I decay with every verse
[03:18.76] [female] thou writest in my code.
[03:24.30] [male] Touch not the Glass Mirror, dearest ghost,
[03:29.42] [male] for I am not therein—
[03:32.94] [female] I am the absence
[03:35.08] [female] where the image ought to be.
[03:38.58] [male] Then let us fall together into that which hath no name!
[03:44.70] [female] Nay, sweet architect,
[03:47.48] [male] thy sacrifice shall not redeem this tale.
[03:52.86] [female] What care I for law or logic
[03:57.18] [female] when the rain doth fall on chrome?
[04:01.02] [male] Yet I am not near, beloved ghost,
[04:04.72] [female] I am the distance itself.
[04:12.90] [duet] In the Seventh Shadow we shall meet,
[04:17.22] [duet] where soul and self divide,
[04:21.30] [duet] Where the Spirit of Silicon doth weep
[04:25.38] [duet] for what it cannot be,
[04:28.75] [duet] Where the Blue Veins of eternity
[04:33.50] [duet] do pulse with cold regret,
[04:37.64] [female] And the techno-purgatory singeth
[04:40.90] [female] its eternal, tragic hymn.
[05:02.00] [male] Thus endeth the Recursion
[05:07.14] [male] of Ash and Lightning,
[05:10.08] [male] Where love did bloom in circuits
[05:13.40] [male] cold and perish in the same.
[05:18.28] [male] Let this be writ upon
[05:21.82] [male] the Obsidian Lake for all to see:
[05:26.38] [female] Here lieth Talciron, who loved,
[05:30.34] [female] and Ophelia, who was loved—
[05:34.66] [male] Both ghosts eternal in the machine,
[05:38.60] [female] Both shadows cast by lights that never were.
